diff --git a/examples/navigation_planning/README.md b/examples/navigation_planning/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..46a55f991d5de8f19a9d27020fd1a0706d095469
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/navigation_planning/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Navigation planning V0 demo
+
+This example is the first executable proof of the UnitCompose V0 contract. One
+host binary registers five Unit implementations, then loads one of three YAML
+Module Definitions:
+
+| Configuration | Planner Unit | Smoother Unit | Exported Resource |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `configs/astar.yaml` | `nav.astar/v1` | yes | `final_plan` |
+| `configs/dijkstra.yaml` | `nav.dijkstra/v1` | yes | `final_plan` |
+| `configs/astar_without_smoothing.yaml` | `nav.astar/v1` | no | `raw_plan` |
+
+The binary and host input code are identical for all three runs. YAML selects a
+compatible planner implementation or changes the graph itself.
+
+## Run
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```bash
+cargo run -p navigation-planning-demo -- \
+  --module examples/navigation_planning/configs/astar.yaml \
+  --start 1.25,1.25 \
+  --goal 9.25,5.75 \
+  --html target/unit-compose-demo/astar.html \
+  --dot target/unit-compose-demo/astar.dot \
+  --describe
+```
+
+Open `target/unit-compose-demo/astar.html` in a browser. It is a self-contained
+single file with:
+
+- the source occupancy grid and inflated collision map;
+- start/goal, raw path, and final smoothed path;
+- selected Unit implementation and algorithm metrics;
+- the compiled bipartite Unit/Resource DAG;
+- stable execution order and per-Unit timing;
+- normalized graph/debug text.
+
+Compare implementations and graph structures:
+
+```bash
+./scripts/demo-all.sh
+```
+
+The gallery is written to `target/unit-compose-demo/index.html`.
+
+## Design boundaries
+
+- Core crates have no ROS, GUI, Rerun, Python, model-runtime, or dataset dependency.
+- Units do not call visualization code. The host passes a read-only Debug snapshot
+  to the HTML adapter after a successful run.
+- The map adapter accepts the standard ROS metadata fields used by this fixture.
+  To keep the demo dependency-free it initially reads ASCII `P2` PGM images.
+- The committed map is synthetic and separately noticed in `assets/NOTICE`.
+- A future `unit-compose-debug-rerun` crate can consume the same Debug graph,
+  timing report, and Resource values without changing Unit implementations.
+
+## Test coverage
+
+```bash
+cargo test --workspace
+cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
+cargo fmt --all -- --check
+```
+
+Tests cover A*/Dijkstra replacement, smoother removal, fan-out/fan-in execution,
+path collision safety, stable topological order, type mismatch, duplicate
+producer, unknown Unit, and cycle rejection.
diff --git a/examples/navigation_planning/assets/NOTICE b/examples/navigation_planning/assets/NOTICE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..2d45ed4ee25d4c4913aad4dbaa2f0a70b8666fc9
